(67, 'An--------- is a company whose main business is holding securities for investment purpose.', '["Banking Company","Producer Company","Investment Company","Financial Company"]'::jsonb, 2, NULL),
(68, 'The Company by its main object in its MOA involved in primary production stated in Section 581 B of Company Act, 1956 is a Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦..', '["Banking Company","Producer Company","Investment Company","Financial Company"]'::jsonb, 1, NULL),
(69, 'Section 8 of the Companies Act, 2013 deals with which type of company -------', '["Banking Company","Investment Company","Financial Company","Non Profit Company"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(70, 'Main object of Non Profit Company', '["Promote art, commerce, science","Social welfare","Protection of environment","All of above"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(71, 'The term Private Company is defined under which section of the Companies Act, 2013?', '["Section 2 (71)","Section 2 (85)","Section 2 (4)","Section 2 (68)"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(72, 'The term One Person Company is defined under which section of the Companies Act, 2013?', '["Section 2 (71)","Section 2 (62)","Section 2 (85)","Section 2 (68)"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(73, 'The term Small Company is defined under which section of the Companies Act, 2013?', '["Section 2 (71)","Section 2 (62)","Section 2 (85)","Section 2 (68)"]'::jsonb, 2, NULL),
(74, 'Which types of resolutions passed in General Meeting?', '["Ordinary","Special","Unanimous","All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(75, 'Creditors Meeting are not normally conducted in the company on very special cases like--------------', '["Winding Up of the Company","Amalgamation, Merger and Reconstruction of the Company","Reduction of capital and changes in Object clause of MOA","All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(76, 'All the votes of present & voting members shall be in favor of resolution, that resolution is called --------', '["Ordinary","Special","Unanimous","None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, NULL),
(77, 'Which of the following businesses are ordinary business?', '["Appointment & remuneration of BOD","Appointment & remuneration of Auditor","Acceptance of Accounts and declaration of dividend","All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(78, 'Meeting of board of directors is called as -------------', '["General meeting","Creditor meeting","Board meeting","None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, NULL),
(79, 'Any business other than ordinary business is special business. True or False.', '["True","False","Partly True","Partly False"]'::jsonb, 0, NULL),
(80, 'Statutory meeting is held after ------ month but before ------------ months from incorporation.', '["1, 6","2, 4","3,4","1, 5"]'::jsonb, 0, NULL),
(81, 'Mr. M held all the shares of the ABC Ltd. except 1. He insured the product C of the company in his own name. Product C is destroyed by fire. Mr. M wants to claim the compensation for the product C destroyed from the company. Whether Mr. M can claim the compensation from the insurance company for loss?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 1, 'As per Section 9 of Companies Act, 2013, (Property of the Company is not the property of the shareholders, it is property of the Company because Company is separate legal entity from shareholders. Insurance company is also at the fault of giving insurance to Mr. M then Mr. M can claim the damages but compensation cannot be claimed'),
(82, 'Legal position of a promoter of a company is Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦.', '["That of an agent","That of a trustee","That of a solicitor","In a fiduciary capacity"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(83, 'P InfoTech Ltd. was registered as a public Limited. There are 76 m embers in the Company, directors and their relatives 3 6 members, employees Ã¢â‚¬â€œ 12, ex - employees 8, 7 couples holding shares jointly 14, and others 6. The board of directors of the company propose to convert it into a private company to public company. State reduction in the number of members?', '["49","62","70","76"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Where 2 or more persons hold one or more shares jointly, they be treated as single member and also person who are in the employment and person who having been formerly in the employment are excluded from membership'),
(84, 'Rajiv owns a garments shop with his two brothers. They decided to diversify their business by creating a company that will manufacture garments. They are facing some financial difficulties in this regard. They collectively have just Rs. 80,000 as capital. Furthermore, they wish to limit their liabilities because of such financial shortcomings. Can they form a private company under such conditions?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Although the Companies Act h ad previously prescribed a minimum capital requirement of Rs. 1 lakh, this is now omitted. Considering the second condition, they can opt for a company limited by shares or guarantee'),
(86, 'Life Insurance Company is which type of company?', '["Statutory Company","Chartered Company","Registered Company","None of the above"]'::jsonb, 0, NULL),
(87, 'ABC Pvt. Ltd., company is a private limited having 5 members only. All the members of the company were going by car in relation to some business. An accident took place and all of them died. Whether existence of the company has also come to the end?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","CanÃ¢â‚¬â„¢t say"]'::jsonb, 1, 'One of the character is separate legal entity i.e. members are separate and company are separate. The stability and perpetuity to the company form business organization'),
(88, 'The Ã¢â‚¬Ëœcommon sealÃ¢â‚¬â„¢ of the company should haveÃ¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦', '["The companyÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s name","The words Ã¢â‚¬Ëœcorporate sealÃ¢â‚¬â„¢","The place of the company","All the above"]'::jsonb, 3, NULL),
(89, 'Power to use official seal of the company outside India is to be authorized by.', '["Article of Association","Memorandum of Association","Both Memorandum and Article of Association","Central Government"]'::jsonb, 0, NULL),
(90, 'East India Company is an example ofÃ¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã¢â‚¬Â¦', '["Statutory Company","Registered company","Chartered company","None of these"]'::jsonb, 2, NULL),
(91, 'H Ltd. holds more than 51% voting power of S Ltd. and also controls composition of R Ltd. Both S and R Ltd. are subsidiaries of H Ltd. S Ltd Holds 30% voting power of P Ltd. and R Ltd. holds 30% voting power of P Ltd. Whether P Ltd. is also subsidiary of H Ltd.?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'As per Section 2(87) of the Company Act, 2013, Company in which holding company exercises or controls more than one - half of the total voting power either its own or together with one or more of its subsidiary companies.( 30% +30%= 60%'),
(92, 'H Ltd. holds more than 51% voting power of S Ltd. and also controls composition of R Ltd. Both S and R Ltd. are subsidiaries of H Ltd. S Ltd Holds 20% voting power of P Ltd., R Ltd. also holds 20% voting power of P Ltd. and also H Ltd. holds 20% voting power of P Ltd. Whether P Ltd. is also subsidiary of H Ltd.?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'As pe r Section 2(87) of the Company Act, 2013, Company in which holding company exercises or controls more than one - half of the total voting power either its own or together with one or more of its subsidiary companies. (20%+20%+20%=60%'),
(93, 'H Ltd. holds more than 51% voting power of S Ltd. and also controls composition of R Ltd. Both S and R Ltd. are subsidiaries of H Ltd. S Ltd controls composition of P Ltd. and R Ltd. also Controls composition of P Ltd. Whether P Ltd. is also subsidiary of H Ltd.?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'As per Section 2(87) of the Company Act, 2013, Company in which holding company controls the composition of the Board of Director or exercises or controls more than one - half of the total voting power either its own or together with one or more of its su bsidiary companies.'),
(94, 'H Ltd. holds more than 50% voting power of S Ltd. and R Ltd controls composition of S Ltd. Whether S Ltd. is subsidiary of both H Ltd. and R Ltd.?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Holding Company have many subsidiary Company at the same time, and also subsidiary Company also have many Holding Company at the same time'),
(98, 'H Ltd. holds more than 51% voting power of S Pvt. Ltd. and also controls composition of R Pvt. Ltd. S Pvt. Ltd. and R Pvt. Ltd. are considered deemed public company. S Pvt. Ltd Holds 30% voting power of P Pvt. Ltd. and R Pvt. Ltd. holds 25% voting power of P Pvt. Ltd. Whether P Pvt. Ltd. is deemed public company?', '["Yes","No","Partly Yes","Partly No"]'::jsonb, 0, 'As per Section 2(87) of the Company Act, 2013, Company in which holding company exercises or controls more than one - half of the total voting power either its own or together with one or more of its subsidiary companies. (30%+25%=55% ) Private Limited Co mpany which is a subsidiary of the Public Limited Company considered as deemed Public Limited Company')
) as v(question_no, question, options, correct_index, hint)
