(26, 'Rule of strict construction should generally be applied in which type of case:', '["criminal case","civil case","labour and welfare case","marriage case"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Strict construction must be applied to Criminal statutes This means that a criminal statute may not be enlarged by implication or intent beyond the fair meaning of the language used or the meaning that is reasonably justified by its terms.'),
(27, 'In which case supreme court observed that principles of interpretation can be applied only if there is an ambiguity in a provision, and not permissible first to create an artificial ambiguity.', '["CIT vi Indian Bank ltd. AIR (1965) SC 1473","Saleh Bros. V K Rajendran and Anr., AIR 1970 Mad 165,","Nagpur Railway Co. Ltd, v. Ruttanp Ramp, AIR 1938 PC 67.","Mercara v. KodimaniandraDeviah, AIR 1962 SC 847."]'::jsonb, 0, 'in case CIT v. Indian Bank ltd. AIR (1965) SC 1473'),
